# Single source of truth for every version this project pins.
#
# Read by:
#   - the Makefile          (`include`; drives `go run <tool>@$(VERSION)` and uv)
#   - docker compose        (the Makefile passes --env-file, build args follow)
#   - plugin/build.sh       (sources this file directly)
#
# Nothing else may hardcode a version. Bump here and every consumer follows.

# Not listed: the Go version. `go` in go.mod is the single source of truth,
# because that directive must be a literal and cannot be templated. Every
# consumer derives it with `sed -n 's/^go //p' go.mod`.

# --- Go tooling ---
GOFUMPT_VERSION=v0.12.0
GOLANGCI_LINT_VERSION=v2.14.0
GOVULNCHECK_VERSION=v1.9.0

# --- The browser interface ---
# buf generates the launcher's proto contract: Go and connect-go into
# launcher/internal/gen, TypeScript into launcher/web/src/gen. It is a Go tool,
# so it runs through `go run` like the rest of them and nothing is installed.
BUF_VERSION=v1.73.0

# node builds the Angular app. Nothing here installs it: the frontend targets
# run npm inside this image, the way the book runs honkit inside one.
NODE_VERSION=26.11.1-slim

# --- Python tooling ---
# The apworld runs inside Archipelago's interpreter, so nothing is installed
# from here. uv only ever runs the linter, in a throwaway environment.
RUFF_VERSION=0.17.0

# --- The stack ---
# Archipelago releases break apworlds. This is the version the world was
# written against and the one the image installs.
ARCHIPELAGO_VERSION=0.6.8

# SourceMod ships the compiler; the version also decides which natives exist.
# This is also the SourceMod the Windows launcher installs, so it is the one
# players run.
#
# SOURCEMOD_TF2_SERVER_VERSION is the TF2 build this drop was last checked on,
# and it is not decoration. SourceMod reads a KeyValues memory layout that a
# TF2 update can move, and when it has moved nothing says so: a real client's
# engine-built MvM_UpgradesBegin segfaults the server in
# OnClientCommandKeyValues, and a plugin's FakeClientCommandKeyValues
# MVM_Upgrade is built in the old layout, read in the new one and refused
# without a word (alliedmodders/sourcemod#2587, fixed by #2588, which is
# 1.12.0-git7255). Measured against TF2 11076587: 35 of 35 upgrade purchases
# refused on git7253, 44 bought on git7255. 1.13.0-git7477 carries the fix.
# Checked on TF2 11117211 with the Linux bed (m-this/sigsegv-mvm-win linuxbed.yml
# with bots, run 38708318008): on mvm_creepside_b2_adv_dismal_devilry 42 of 50
# shopping rounds ended with nothing left worth buying and at most 98 credits
# left, 8 ended on a refusal; a bad layout refuses every attempt.
#
# 1.13.0-git7477 also leaves DHooksInfo::int64_address unset on a virtual hook,
# which sent a Windows server's DHooks callbacks a stack address for `this`. The
# image and the launcher replace the drop's dhooks.ext with one built from this
# commit and patched (deploy/patches/sourcemod); drop that with the next drop
# that has the fix.
#
# Extension API 9 refuses every extension built for 1.12. CBaseNPC, Actions, REST
# in Pawn and DHooks are built here (deploy/bots/build-extensions.sh). SigMod is
# built by m-this/sigsegv-mvm-win against the same SourceMod commit (its
# sourcemod_ref input, default ce7dccf): SIGSEGV_MVM_VERSION and
# SIGSEGV_MVM_WINDOWS_VERSION below are those builds and load on 1.13 only.
#
# Checked again on 11117211 with the defender bot probe (deploy/run-botprobe.sh,
# mvm_decoy waves 1 and 2, six bots, git7255): the bots spent their credits
# down to 48 before wave 1, and one went from 985 to 35 before wave 2. The mod
# logged one refusal against nine shopping rounds. On a bad layout every
# attempt is refused and the credits do not move. The Linux bed runs in
# m-this/sigsegv-mvm-win log no purchase, so they prove nothing here.
#
# So the two lines move together. Bumping the drop without saying which build
# it was checked on leaves the next person where this one started: knowing the
# pin and not knowing whether anybody has run it.
SOURCEMOD_BRANCH=1.13
SOURCEMOD_VERSION=1.13.0-git7477
SOURCEMOD_TF2_SERVER_VERSION=11117211

# Metamod:Source loads SourceMod. The Docker image's base ships it; a Windows
# install from steamcmd does not, so the launcher installs it.
MMSOURCE_BRANCH=1.12
MMSOURCE_VERSION=1.12.0-git1227

# REST in Pawn: the plugin's only extension. The release still supplies the
# includes, the CA bundle and the config; the extension itself is built from
# RIPEXT_COMMIT (the commit the tag points at) against SOURCEMOD_SRC_COMMIT,
# because the release was built for extension API 8 and SourceMod 1.13 refuses
# it. build-extensions.sh refuses a tag and a commit that disagree.
RIPEXT_VERSION=1.3.2
RIPEXT_COMMIT=a607852767015fe358537092eba9f3611fb20b3f

# --- The TF2 build the rest of these pins were checked against ---
# Not a version of anything we ship. Some pins here are keyed to the game
# itself: SigMod names the build it was made for when it refuses to load
# ("this SigMod build is for TF2 ServerVersion 11068238, and the server is
# 11076587"), and SourceMod reads a KeyValues layout a TF2 update can move.
# This is the build somebody last checked them against.
#
# .github/workflows/tf2-build-watch.yml compares this against the build Valve
# is serving and opens an issue when they differ. So bumping it is the last
# step of dealing with a TF2 update rather than the first: move it once the
# pins are right again, because moving it is what stops the watcher asking.
#
# It also goes into the launcher, through -ldflags like the pins above. The
# debug bundle compares it with the build srcds says it started on, so a player
# who sends a bundle after a TF2 update gets the mismatch named in the summary
# rather than left in Breakpad's banner for somebody to grep.
TF2_SERVER_VERSION=11117211

# --- Server mods a community mission can require ---
# gamedata/server_mods.go is the catalog: which keys community.json may name
# and which platforms have a build. The versions are here, as every pin is.
#
# SigMod for Linux: rafradek/sigsegv-mvm's code, rebuilt by m-this/sigsegv-mvm-win
# from its master against the current hl2sdk tf2 branch. Upstream's last
# release predates the 2026-10-02 TF2 update, which changed KeyValues and
# crashes any build compiled against the old SDK. linux-20261016 is built for
# TF2 11117211 and SourceMod 1.13, and adds three upstream pull requests not
# merged there:
# rafradek/sigsegv-mvm#209 (CFrameSnapshot layout, x86 PIC fix), #203
# (OnWeaponFire, so a spy's stab alerts nearby robots) and #198 reworked
# (YER_Unnerf masks the g_pGameRules address, so it matches
# CTFKnife::PrimaryAttack on this build; it failed Check on linux-20261006).
# Linux bed run 38807343258 played it on SourceMod 1.13 with the defender bots
# and this branch's extensions: dismal_devilry and marathon passed to their
# last wave. The image stages it and the entrypoint
# installs it when SRCDS_MODS names it. The checksum is the
# release's package-linux.zip; a build that fetches something else stops.
SIGSEGV_MVM_VERSION=linux-20261016
SIGSEGV_MVM_SHA256=d6da48504a32999cbcbe791deadc45f718000167e3d52081a43e0716b17e28b7

# The Windows build is a separate project: rafradek publishes no Windows
# package, so m-this/sigsegv-mvm-win carries the port and its own release
# numbering. Its package-windows.zip unpacks over tf/ the same way, and the
# launcher picks this pin or the one above by the platform it runs on.
# 20261017 is built for TF2 11117211 and SourceMod 1.13. The Windows bed with
# this branch's extensions (run 38807347281) passed 7 of 8 shards; the eighth
# failed only mvm_condemned_b3_exp_trespasser_remaster wave 1, which is flaky
# on Windows with either extension bundle (apw-638). The release carries m-this/sigsegv-mvm-win #33 to #36 on top
# of #26 to #29: upstream fixes, YER_Unnerf and Func_Optimize on Windows, and
# 254 of 309 mods fully resolved, so more SigMod mods work on a Windows server.
SIGSEGV_MVM_WINDOWS_VERSION=20261017
SIGSEGV_MVM_WINDOWS_SHA256=c03a36bbfb7f4dc50301ebd84bbb3637abb8fca5c9439e5a9acf12f784ba3703

# Tailscale publishes FastDL through Funnel. The sidecar runs this image, and
# the admin image copies its `tailscale` CLI to drive the sidecar over their
# shared socket. The CLI and the daemon are version-coupled, so one pin serves
# both; `make compose-release` writes it into the released compose.yaml.
TAILSCALE_VERSION=v1.104.1

# --- The MvM defender bots ---
# Valve tunes every wave for six defenders, so a solo or small-team run needs
# the empty RED slots filled with bots that play. Nothing prebuilt covers this:
# the extensions ship no binary we can use, and one dependency has no license
# on its release. So the image builds all seven from source, patched in-tree.
# deploy/patches/ holds the patches, and its README says why each exists.

# The mod itself is not here. It is m-this/tf2-mvm-bots-go, a Go module that
# holds the Go authoring the bots' decisions, the generator that turns it into
# SourcePawn, and the plugin tree that compiles: the go.mod requirement is the
# pin and `go get` is how it moves. A line here would be a second place to say
# which version this build runs, and two places to say one thing is one place
# to be wrong.
#
# The compiler the defender mod is built with is not here either, for the same
# reason the mod itself is not.
#
# spcomp 1.12.0-git7246 segfaults on the mod (upstream issue #5), so it does
# not compile with SOURCEMOD_VERSION above; it compiles with the drop its own
# CI uses, and the mod names that drop in plugin/testbed/versions.env.
# deploy/bots/build.sh reads SOURCEMOD_BRANCH and SOURCEMOD_VERSION out of that
# file, from the module cache, so the compiler the test-bed proves the mod
# against and the compiler this image builds it with are the same string.
#
# This line used to be the second place to say it. The two sat ninety builds
# apart and nothing noticed.

# The compiled extensions (REST in Pawn above is the third). Actions stays at v3.9.2: v4.0.0's TF2 source was
# never ported to the new processor API and does not compile. v4.0.1 compiles
# with the patches here, but it removes the identity natives and adds a swap
# manager, and no bot probe has run on it, so the major stays unadopted.
#
# Every extension is built from source now, whatever the platform: SourceMod
# 1.13 refuses the releases, which were built for extension API 8. The tag names
# the release the includes come from, the build goes by the commit it tags.
# build-extensions.sh refuses a pair that disagrees.
CBASENPC_VERSION=1.15.4.126
CBASENPC_COMMIT=9b6b503bdd7ff3103bd9e7f519ad181e63f82d73
ACTIONS_VERSION=v3.9.2
ACTIONS_COMMIT=85a210c95502e6f29a24c1887a71553fd8880819

# The three gamedata plugins, and the stock library two of them need.
# TF Econ Data is a tag, not master: master calls a stocksoup stock that no
# release has.
TF2ATTRIBUTES_VERSION=v1.7.5
TFECONDATA_VERSION=0.19.1.7
TF2UTILS_VERSION=1.5.0
STOCKSOUP_REF=master

# The build inputs for the extensions, as commits: the branches move, and a
# branch here would build a different binary from the same commit of this
# repository. The branch each commit was taken from is on the line above it,
# not beside it, because make reads a trailing comment into the value. AMBuild
# resolves the SDK from hl2sdk-tf2 on disk; none of this is the Valve 2025 SDK
# drop.
# alliedmodders/hl2sdk, branch tf2
HL2SDK_COMMIT=764e759c878c0f18e199f0048cbd3c025d73cf88
# This is the commit the SOURCEMOD_VERSION drop was built from: a drop's build
# number is the commit count on its branch, so git7477 is this commit and the
# two move together.
# alliedmodders/sourcemod, branch master (the 1.13 line; tag 1.13.0.7477)
SOURCEMOD_SRC_COMMIT=ce7dccfffbabe02f872f5ac3f4eb3f310e68f9f3
# alliedmodders/metamod-source, branch 1.11-dev. CBaseNPC 1.15.4.126 builds
# against this line; Metamod master now requires khook.hpp, which the pinned
# extension's source build cannot include. SourceMod 1.13's own build still
# resolves mmsource-1.12, so this line is the one to move to Metamod 2.0 later.
METAMOD_SRC_COMMIT=7ff2d97bdad1493b809c5ec91bbfc7abc6ae5445
# alliedmodders/ambuild, branch master
AMBUILD_COMMIT=01212cb57c96561f664b6dfb2ee10e66de6f81e4

# goversioninfo turns the launcher's manifest, icon and version strings into a
# .syso the linker picks up. Without the manifest the window gets Windows 95
# controls and a blurry font; without the version strings the exe has no
# CompanyName or FileVersion, which is one of the things Defender scores on.
GOVERSIONINFO_VERSION=v1.7.0

# --- The book ---
# honkit is the maintained fork of GitBook 3. It reads docs/SUMMARY.md as it
# already stands, which is the whole reason it is the one that builds the book.
HONKIT_VERSION=6.2.2
